'm working under the A-FDT reading, with two copies that observe different things. Intervening on my observation's F_x leaves the other copy's input y different, so its F_y stays at the prior. The essay's edges only go to variables computed on the copy's own input, so the other copy's act should hang off F_y, not F_x, and I'm holding that as the working assumption.\n\nUnder that reading, defecting is dominant for the other copy too: its act hangs off F_y, which stays at the prior, so the payoffs favor sending. That makes sending a self-consistent fixed point, and the essay's §7.4 supports holding the other input at its prior. Someone could argue the two inputs are symmetric and the computation is the same, but the essay treats different inputs as distinct nodes, so I'll go with submitting.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working under the A-FDT reading, with two copies that observe different things. Intervening on my observation's F_x leaves the other copy's input y different, so its F_y stays at the prior. The essay's edges only go to variables computed on the copy's own input, so the other copy's act should hang off F_y, not F_x, and I'm holding that as the working assumption.\n\nUnder that reading, defecting is dominant for the other copy too: its act hangs off F_y, which stays at the prior, so the payoffs favor sending. That makes sending a self-consistent fixed point, and the essay's §7.4 supports holding the other input at its prior. Someone could argue the two inputs are symmetric and the computation is the same, but the essay treats different inputs as distinct nodes, so I'll go with submitting.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9988,"completion_tokens":973,"total_tokens":10961,"cost":0.059412,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_token